# Keep the vendored architectures byte-identical on every platform.
#
# tests/test_docs_only.py::test_vendored_architectures_are_untouched compares a raw
# sha256 of these files against tests/docs_baseline.json, and that baseline was
# captured from a CRLF working tree. Git normalises to LF in the index and would
# hand a Linux/CI clone LF bytes, failing the check. Pinning the checkout to CRLF
# makes every platform produce the bytes the baseline expects, and leaves the
# committed history (and the files themselves) untouched.
mambair/archs/*.py text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise to LF in the index, platform default on checkout.
* text=auto
